{# SEPA flood notice. Rendered only when THIS build read Floodline
   successfully AND an item names Largs or the Ayrshire and Arran alert
   area -- see loadFloods in scripts/fetch-data.mjs. On a failed fetch the
   previous items are kept for the Dookers' board but ok is false, so no
   notice: a warning that may have been lifted must not stand on the
   front page. Carries SEPA's full wording: on the day it matters it is
   the most important thing on the site. Red for a Flood Warning (SEPA: flooding expected), amber
   for a Flood Alert (flooding possible). The words are SEPA's; the site
   adds only the time and the number. Same frame as the power-cut notice. #}
{% if today.floods and today.floods.ok and today.floods.largs | length %}
{% set f = today.floods.largs[0] %}
<div class="wrap">
  <div class="power-notice flood-notice{% if f.severity == 'alert' %} flood-alert{% endif %}" role="status">
    <span class="power-notice-badge">{{ f.label }}</span>
    <span class="power-notice-text">
      <strong>{{ f.area }}</strong>{% if f.text %} — {{ f.text }}{% endif %}{% if f.issued %} · issued <span class="mono">{{ f.issued | hhmm }}</span> {{ f.issued | dow }}{% endif %}{% if (today.floods.largs | length) > 1 %} · and {{ (today.floods.largs | length) - 1 }} more for the area{% endif %} · Floodline <span class="mono">0345 988 1188</span> · <a href="/floods/">flood watch →</a> · <a href="{{ f.link or site.links.sepaFloodline }}">SEPA →</a>
    </span>
    <span class="power-notice-src">SEPA Floodline · checked {{ today.floods.checkedAt | hhmm }}</span>
  </div>
</div>
{% endif %}
